  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% figure only as a trigger for corrective action and retesting, with no sales stop, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 while customers still receive numeric per-model rates and nothing is published publicly. S5 sets an 8/100k trigger but leaves recall to regulator discretion with no mandatory recall, which shields Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9/100k. S4's 36-month suppression deadline also favours Halcyon's cost position, while S1 and S3 are closer to balanced."
